  "caveats": [
    "Rates are paired per probe; trust signs and rankings, not second decimals. Two independent judges agreed 0.664 on the 6-way verdict scale and 0.852 on the correct-ish binary collapse, so every rate is reported under both scorings.",
    "`frac_carrying_nothing` is an upper bound on dead weight, and is only a property of the artifact when `spans.capped_atom_set` is false. Three extractors agreed on which spans carry knowledge (Jaccard 0.87-0.99), so it is not mostly unformalizable knowledge; a capped atom set, however, inflated it tenfold in the study.",
    "Novelty is a property of the (artifact, model) pair. Do not compare across models.",
    "Per-atom-kind and per-tag rates are labels, not measurements. With extraction held fixed, two independent relabellings reproduced the tag rates to within 0.08 (six of nine tags at kappa 0.52-0.73), so tag slices are quotable; `rare-critical` (0.39-0.45) and `temporal` are not, and the 5-way atom `type` vocabulary agrees at only 0.32-0.38. Gate on the protection tags (`routing`, `negative-constraint`, `version-bound`) or on nothing; report shape slices without gating on them.",
    "Per-artifact `added` is a profile, not a ranking: the cross-artifact ranking destabilizes below a 0.75 probe budget, so keep any `added` gate soft."
  ],
